## Phase 1 — Consumer and Lite trace namespace parity
- Replaced configured-namespace removal with Java's one-argument NamespaceUtil operation in General Consumer and Lite group/topic trace fields.
- Lite now stores a once-normalized before group and derives SubAfter by normalizing that snapshot again; callback-time group mutation remains ignored.
- Added regression cases for foreign and nested prefixes, absent/configured namespaces, null/empty groups, retry/DLQ topics, and system resources; General Consumer verifies its nested two-stage group and foreign topic.
- Validation: cargo fmt --all; cargo test --offline --locked -p rocketmq-classic-consumer -p rocketmq-classic-producer trace (Consumer trace tests passed; full final gates remain).

## Phase 2 — Producer trace namespace parity
- Send, EndTransaction, and Recall trace builders now remove any resource namespace independently of ClientConfig, matching Java's overload; host-client ID remains derived from ClientConfig where required.
- Regression tests assert public group  and Pub topic normalization without configured namespace, plus foreign-prefix EndTransaction and Recall group/topic values.
- Validation: cargo test --offline --locked -p rocketmq-classic-producer trace (9 unit tests and 3 trace lifecycle integration tests passed); cargo fmt --all -- --check; git diff --check.
